This project could help improve the safety of AI-powered self-driving cars by studying how accurately
their cameras detect objects under different conditions. By testing factors such as blur, low resolution,
brightness, missing frames, and different weather conditions, we can identify when AI vision systems become
less reliable. The results could help researchers and engineers understand which conditions pose the
greatest risks for detecting important objects such as pedestrians, bicycles, and other vehicles. This
information could be used to improve camera systems, data-quality monitoring, and safety measures in
autonomous vehicles. Ultimately, the project could contribute to making self-driving technology more
reliable and safer for people sharing the road.
